        "main_image": "shopify://shop_images/magnific_generate-this-man.png",
        "heading": "<p>CELLULAR ENERGY,<br/>RECOVERY &<br/>PERFORMANCE<br/>EXPLAINED</p>",
        "heading_tag": "h2",
        "content": "<p>Every cell runs its own daily protocol: produce, protect, put to work - and the mitochondria are the engines behind it, converting what you eat into the energy currency every cell runs on.</p><p>With enough NAD⁺ to draw on, that protocol runs properly: energy gets made, damage gets repaired, recovery happens overnight, and performance keeps building instead of resetting.</p><p>NAD⁺ supply starts falling from your mid-thirties, and by 40 it's roughly half what it was - so the rebuild slows, afternoons flatten, and recovery quietly takes longer. </p><p>Most people feel it before a blood test ever would.</p>",
