    "custom_faqs_7VcJGf": {
      "type": "custom-faqs",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_BQAJKd": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What ingredients does MUTO contain?",
            "content": "<p>Fifteen ingredients, working as one system rather than fifteen separate add-ons. At the core is Nicotinamide Riboside, the ingredient your body converts directly into NAD+, supported by CoQ10, Pterostilbene, Quercetin, Grape Seed Extract, Turmeric Extract, a methylated B-complex, Zinc, Copper, Vitamin D3, K2 and BioPerine for absorption, together feeding all six of the body's NAD+ pathways. Full doses are disclosed on our Science page. Nothing hidden behind a proprietary blend.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_FbwF6B": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can MUTO replace my current supplement stack?",
            "content": "<p>For most people, yes. MUTO is built to replace a typical seven-product cellular stack, NAD+ support, B vitamins, minerals, antioxidants, polyphenols, vitamins D3 & K2, in two capsules a day. That works out to around £45 a month versus £120 a month buying each one separately, a saving of roughly £75 a month. If you're taking something specific to a medical condition, check with your doctor before stopping it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_RcHdm7": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "When will I feel a difference?",
            "content": "<p>Most people notice steadier energy within the first week, with recovery starting to improve by around day 30. By day 60 to 90, the shift usually shows up in your wearable data too: HRV and resting heart rate are validated markers of cellular recovery. MUTO compounds rather than resets, so the longer you stay on it, the stronger your baseline gets.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_KFUWda": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do I need to cycle on and off MUTO?",
            "content": "<p>No. MUTO isn't a stimulant, so there's no tolerance to build and nothing to cycle off from. It's designed for daily, ongoing use. The benefits build the longer you stay consistent, not fade the longer you take it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_VVKQgq": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I take MUTO with other supplements?",
            "content": "<p>Generally, yes. MUTO is formulated to work alongside most everyday supplements. The one thing to watch is significant overlap, like a separate NAD+ or B-vitamin product, where you'd risk doubling up rather than adding anything. If you're on prescription medication, check with your doctor first.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_VOKQnj": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is MUTO safe for children or pregnant women?",
            "content": "<p>MUTO is formulated for adults and isn't intended for anyone under 18. If you're pregnant, breastfeeding, or trying to conceive, please speak to your doctor before taking MUTO or any new supplement.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
